04:47.920 --> 04:48.880
So let's go and do it.

04:48.880 --> 04:50.280
I'm going to put it at the end.

04:50.280 --> 04:57.440
So score plus ten and let's give it the name score with bonus.

04:58.240 --> 04:58.920
So that's it.

04:58.920 --> 05:00.280
Let's go and execute it.

05:00.280 --> 05:01.960
So now in the output you can see it's very easy.

05:02.000 --> 05:04.160
We have added a ten for each score.

05:04.360 --> 05:07.480
So we have increased the score points for each customer.

05:07.480 --> 05:09.180
But now for the last customer.

05:09.220 --> 05:14.980
Anna, you can see over here she doesn't have a value in the scores and that's why SQL didn't go and

05:14.980 --> 05:15.580
add it in.

05:15.580 --> 05:17.300
So we will get as well a null.

05:17.340 --> 05:21.940
And of course, this might not be fair that the last customer is not getting any point, even though

05:21.940 --> 05:23.700
that we have increased for all others.

05:23.700 --> 05:28.020
So that means we have to go and handle the null by replacing the null to zero.

05:28.020 --> 05:31.020
And only after that we're going to add a plus to it.

05:31.020 --> 05:32.220
So let's go and do that.

05:32.220 --> 05:33.820
I'm going to add a coalesce.

05:35.860 --> 05:39.020
If it is null then go and make it zero.

05:39.020 --> 05:41.820
And afterwards go and add a ten points.

05:41.820 --> 05:43.500
So let's go and execute it.

05:43.500 --> 05:49.740
So now as you can see the results everything now is fair where we have a ten bonus points for each customers.

05:49.740 --> 05:53.700
Even if the customer doesn't have any values in the scores like here.

05:53.740 --> 05:57.260
Anna, she has like null, but still she is getting a ten points.

05:57.260 --> 06:02.580
So here again, as you can see, if you don't handle the nulls correctly before doing the mathematical

06:02.580 --> 06:05.620
operations, you might get unexpected results.

06:05.620 --> 06:10.380
So be careful with the nulls and handle them correctly before adding anything.
